**Memo**

**To:** All Staff  
**From:** Jennifer L. Martinez, Senior Vice President of Property Management  
**Date:** October 15, 2023  
**Subject:** Quarterly Report on Properties, Developments, Leasing, and Valuations  

As we approach the end of Q3 2023, I want to take this opportunity to provide an update on our property portfolio, ongoing developments, leasing activities, and valuation assessments. Our overall performance reflects the hard work and dedication of our team and highlights opportunities for growth in the real estate market.

**1. Overview of Current Properties**

Our current portfolio consists of 25 properties across the Greater New York area, with a total managed space of 1.5 million square feet. Notably, our flagship property, the Hudson River Plaza, located at 123 West 34th Street, has seen a 15% increase in occupancy year-over-year, now standing at an impressive 92%. The recent renovations, which included energy-efficient windows and modernized common areas, have significantly boosted tenant satisfaction.

We continue to manage properties for several key clients, including the Greenstone Group and Apex Holdings. The successful collaboration with Apex has enabled us to streamline our maintenance processes through the implementation of the Property Management System (PMS) called ProManage, which has reduced response times to tenant requests by 30%. 

**2. Development Projects**

Our development team, led by Project Manager Stephen Chen, is currently overseeing three major projects. The first is the Riverwalk Residences, a luxury condominium development located at 456 River Road, which is set to break ground in December 2023. Construction is projected to complete by December 2025. The project is backed by a partnership with Urban Innovations LLC and has received favorable zoning approvals from the City Council of New York.

Additionally, the team is in the planning stages for the Beacon Heights Office Complex in Long Island City, a 200,000 square foot Class A office building designed to attract tech companies. We are collaborating with the architectural firm, Skyline Architects, and expect to commence construction in early 2024.

**3. Leasing Activities**

Leasing activity remains strong, with a total of 150,000 square feet leased in Q3 2023 alone. The leasing team, headed by Senior Leasing Manager, Maria Gonzalez, has secured notable tenants, including TechWave Solutions, which has signed a five-year lease for 40,000 square feet at the Beacon Tower in Midtown. This lease not only strengthens our tenant mix but also enhances our position in the competitive tech sector.

In light of the upcoming lease expirations at the Riverside Business Center, we are actively negotiating with potential tenants. The team is utilizing our market analysis reports from Property Insights, which provide critical data on local rental trends and vacancy rates. The current average rental rate in the area is $55 per square foot, which is slightly above our projected rates, indicating a favorable market for negotiations.

**4. Property Management Enhancements**

In response to feedback from tenants at the Park Avenue Suites, we have initiated a comprehensive property management enhancement plan. This plan focuses on improving tenant engagement through the launch of a new tenant portal powered by TenantConnect. This platform will allow tenants to submit maintenance requests, access building information, and communicate with property managers more effectively. The pilot program will be rolled out by the end of Q4 2023.

Moreover, our team has been actively engaged in sustainability initiatives. We are in partnership with EcoSmart Solutions to implement energy-saving measures across our properties, aiming for a 20% reduction in energy consumption by 2025.

**5. Valuation Assessments**

As of October 2023, our in-house valuation team, led by Chief Valuation Officer, Dr. Robert Liu, has completed assessments on all properties in our portfolio. The overall portfolio valuation has increased by 10% compared to Q2 2023, due in part to the rising demand for residential properties and the successful leasing of previously vacant spaces.

The valuation of Hudson River Plaza was particularly noteworthy, with an estimated market value now at $125 million, reflecting the renovations and increased occupancy rates. This valuation is critical as we prepare for potential refinancing options with our banking partner, First National Bank, which has shown interest in supporting our growth initiatives.

**6. Future Outlook**

Looking ahead, our focus will remain on maximizing property performance and seeking new development opportunities. The commercial real estate market is anticipated to experience fluctuations, but our diverse portfolio and proactive management strategies position us well for sustained success.

As part of our strategic planning, we will be holding a meeting on October 30, 2023, to discuss our long-term goals and how each team can contribute to our overall vision. I encourage all departments to come prepared with ideas on how we can enhance our service offerings and market presence.

In closing, I want to extend my gratitude to everyone for your hard work and dedication. Together, we are building a robust foundation for our company’s future, and I am excited about the opportunities that lie ahead.

Best regards,

